10984705,2024-12-01,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"I am writing to dispute an error on my TransUnion credit report regarding my XXXX XXXX  account. TransUnion is reporting late payments on this account, but my XXXX credit report accurately reflects that the account was paid on time and closed with no late payments. This discrepancy violates the principle of uniformity of credit reports as outlined in 15 U.S.C. 1681a, which mandates that consumer reporting agencies ensure accurate and consistent reporting of consumer information.

Additionally, this inaccurate reporting constitutes a violation of my rights under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), specifically : 15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ), which requires consumer reporting agencies to maintain reasonable procedures to ensure maximum accuracy of the information in credit reports.

