10985370,2024-12-01,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am writing to dispute the accuracy of an account reported by CB/VICSCredit on my credit report. Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), I have the right to accurate, complete, and verifiable information. Additionally, under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ), I am entitled to protection from misleading debt collection practices. Below are the issues I have identified : XXXX. Inconsistent Reporting Across Bureaus : The High Credit amounts differ across bureaus : {$480.00} ( TransUnion ), {$340.00} ( XXXX ), and {$0.00} ( XXXX ). Additionally, the Account Open Date is inconsistent. These discrepancies violate 15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ). 
