11033390,2024-12-04,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",Mobile or digital wallet,Fraud or scam,,"On XX/XX/year>, I noticed a pending transfer in the amount of {$81.00} from my bank checking account to a PayPal vendor that was clearly fraudulent. I contacted the bank to initiate a stop payment and then contacted PayPal. On that call, we established that someone had hacked my account several months previous and had removed my email credentials and replaced them with their own ; they had also changed the default language on the account from English to Spanish, a language I do not speak. The hacker had made several small transactions ( some for {$0.00} and {$1.00} ) in previous months which I had not noticed, a transaction for {$9.00} on XX/XX/XXXX and another for {$11.00} on XX/XX/XXXX and then the transaction for {$81.00} on XX/XX/XXXX which I had reported immediately. To protect my account against more fraud, we removed all connections to my bank account and credit cards. I was told to leave the account otherwise active so that a refund of the fraudulent charges could be made. Within XXXX days of the call, PayPal, unable to pull the funds from my bank account, proceeded to charge my credit card for {$81.00}. I then called my credit card company, XXXX, to report that this was a fraudulent charge. 

