Sincerely, [ Signature if on paper ] XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX : Copy of the credit report with the reinserted item highlighted [ Other supporting documents ] Summary of Section 611 of the Fair Credit Reporting Act Section 611 of the FCRA outlines the procedures that credit reporting agencies must follow when disputes arise over the accuracy of information in consumer reports.

Key points of Section 611 : Reinvestigation of disputed information : If a consumer disputes the accuracy of any information on their report, the agency must conduct a free reinvestigation to determine if the information is inaccurate. 

Timeline for reinvestigation : The agency must complete the reinvestigation within 30 days of receiving the dispute. 

Notification of results : After the reinvestigation, the agency must provide the consumer with the results and an updated copy of the report if changes were made. 

Reinsertion of deleted information : If information is removed from the report and later reinserted, the agency must notify the consumer in writing within five business days of the reinsertion. 

Procedures to prevent reappearance of information : Agencies must maintain reasonable procedures to ensure that deleted information does not reappear on the report without proper verification.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",TX,75252,,Web,2024-12-27,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
